# issue #51 gears (bsrl-sim), a diff on top of the other patches (on top of heal_scale.patch).
# Two gears per player (gear_boosts.csv, data type 62) in the player config (+0x18 / +0x20), where libg looks for them.
# nbenv_proto.h / py/nbpc: NbeDiv.gear[16][2] (RESET), NbeResp gear_valid / gear_id / gear_shield / gear_stat (every
# response); instance.set_div takes div "gear". offline.c my_player_ctor -> gear.c gear_equip (table 62, allowed for the
# character by libg's 0xae2aa4, not two of a kind; else div_err). battle_fix.c ensure() builds libg's gear instances
# (char+0xd68) for every LogicType 0-18 (was 0 / 1), so libg's own readers run: HealthRegen, SuperChargeRate,
# GadgetCooldown (and SuperHealth, SuperRange, SuperShield, PetDamage, ExtraSpawnling, unverified). gear.c re-implements
# what is compiled out: LowHealthDamage and ConsumableShield (env.c my_root), ForestSpeed (env.c rec_move, a bush change
# re-sends the move), ReloadSpeed (superfix_status.c my_reload_pct); NB_GEARS=0 turns those four off. build.sh: gear.c.
# Notes: notes/issue51.md. Paths relative to engine/.
